  title "The Mirror's Cracked Face"
  summary "At a council meeting in Hearth Plaza, the Light-Regent Xouhoulong faces pressure from E'frostlings delegate Angmo xang'Oath, who demands recognition of territorial gains at the Veil Vents and control of fire-core allocations. Auditor Qeihong reveals that orca raiders are threatening harvesting fleets and that someone has already begun negotiating with the Midnight Claws for passage through the Berg's deep tunnels. Xouhoulong and Qeihong convince Angmo to witness the authentication of a formal compact granting the Midnight Claws diplomatic access and protected passage, framed as a solution to the raiding crisis. Shortly after the compact is sealed with the Directrix Mirror, a catastrophic Calving tears open the eastern ice, killing many including Xouhoulong's companion Selka; Xouhoulong resigns and Qeihong assumes power as Grand Auditor, with the fire-cores continuing to flow under uncertain circumstances."
